description: Bump pyproject.toml version on every PR. CI fails otherwise.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Bump package version on every PR

`pr-checks.yml` requires `[project].version` in `pyproject.toml` to be **strictly greater** than `origin/main`. Merge to `main` publishes that version to PyPI.

When opening, updating, or pushing a PR branch:

1. Read `version` from `origin/main:pyproject.toml` (not the local file if it may already have been bumped).
2. If this branch is not greater, bump the **patch** (`0.1.66` → `0.1.67`). Use minor/major only for a real API break.
3. Include the bump in the same commit or PR as the work. Do not open a follow-up just to bump.

Skip only when the PR does not change anything that ships (no `overmind/`, `skills/`, or `pyproject.toml` code). Skill and CLI changes **do** ship — bump them.

```toml
# ❌ BAD — same as main
version = "0.1.66"

# ✅ GOOD — patch above main
version = "0.1.67"
```
